    'floor(x)+frac(x)=x gives A; floor(frac(x))=0 and frac(floor(x))=0 both give B on R.',
    'The third is zero, not the diagonal A.'],
  ['q720-plane-sets', 'ABC',
    'All three source sets use actual shaded figures and retain free coordinates, half-open edges and corner membership. The border/line conventions are representation scaffolding, not solved condition annotations. Drawing is lost.',
    'floor(x)=0 gives [0,1) times R, the vertical strip A with free y.',
    'floor(y)=1 gives R times [1,2), the horizontal strip B with free x.',
    'The conjunction gives [1,2) times [2,3), exactly rectangle C.',
    'Only the lower-left corner belongs to this rectangle; right/top coordinate boundaries are excluded.',
    'Every x in [0,1), such as .5, is allowed; the set is not a line.'],
  ['q721-tiled-set', 'AC',
    'The source graph of equal floors becomes interpretation of the actual repeating half-open tiles. Infinite integer union, interior membership and mixed boundaries are retained. No finite five-tile truncation is imposed.',
    'Equal floors mean both coordinates are in the same [n,n+1), giving exactly the displayed infinite union.',
    'The off-diagonal interior point (.2,.8) is included, so a line is insufficient.',
    'Both .2,.8 have floor zero; every integer diagonal pair has equal floors and belongs to the next tile.',
    'For x=.9,y=1.1 the coordinate gap is .2<1 but floors 0 and 1 differ.',
    'The condition allows all same-tile interiors, visibly shaded, not just edges.'],
  ['q722-exponent-laws', 'ABDE',
    'All four original expressions retain a,b and root orders. Products, ordinary powers and fractional powers are distinguished with no intermediate exponent already supplied in the stem.',
    'Multiplication of powers with base 10 adds a+b.',
    'Cubing multiplies a by 3.',
    'A square root multiplies b by 1/2, not by 2.',
    'The positive square root of 10^b is 10^(b/2).',
    'The two exponents are 2a/3 and b/5, added under multiplication.',
    'The product exponent is a+b, not ab.'],
  ['q723-positive-powers', 'B',
    'REVISION REQUIRED: both requested numerical graphical estimates are present, but their discrimination is lost. Since 1<1.95^(1/5)<1.95, A/D first entries are below 1 and C first entry is the unchanged input; B is the sole admissible first entry. No graph, inverse reading, numerical exponent or estimate of the second expression is needed to select it. This deletes the key quantitative graph-reading task, beyond ordinary elimination between plausible graphical estimates.',
    'The first power exceeds 1 and the second exceeds 1; both listed estimates violate these basic ranges and cannot fit .02 graph error.',
    'The reused independent graph/numeric evidence gives about 1.14 and 13.6; 14 is compatible with the explicit .02 reading allowance and appropriate coarse precision.',
    'The powers differ substantially from unchanged bases; the first is near 1.14, not 1.95, far beyond allowed graph error.',
    'The first .39 is below 1 despite a base above 1; the second 19 is far from about 13.6 and is not a compatible paired estimate.'],
  ['q723-small-and-product', 'A',
    'REVISION REQUIRED: since .0041<(.0041)^(2/3)<1, B first entry exceeds 1 and C/D first entries are below .0041; A alone satisfies the elementary range. The graph and the product estimate are dispensable. The coarse numerical values are mathematically compatible, but the source quantitative graph-reading/combined-power workflow is not assessed by these distractors.',
    'The reused independent graph evidence gives about .026 and 5.2; both are compatible with the explicit reading tolerance and coarse precision.',
    '39 is outside (0,1) for the first expression; .19 is also far below the actual combined positive-power estimate.',
    '.0027 is below the original base, whereas a subunit base raised to a positive exponent below 1 becomes larger. Thus the pair fails regardless of the second value.',
    '.0026 likewise violates that range; 2.4 is also far from about 5.2.'],
  ['q724-lookup-table', 'C',
    'The original numerical-table inverse task is retained with an explicitly authored eight-entry replacement, not claimed historical source/table identity. Normalization, nearest mantissa and approximate equality are explicit. Precision is reduced to .01 exponents versus the frozen reference-table .0001 readings; original-table use/interpolation and free lookup production are lost, but table inversion and decade shifts remain. Values require comparison of distances, not copying an exact target cell.',
    'The mantissa exponents are selected correctly but decade shifts -1,+1,+2 for the last three inputs are omitted.',
    'For .373=10^-1*3.73, the exponent is -1+.57=-.43, not -.57.',
    'Nearest mantissa columns are .20,.57,.71,.30; adding the decade characteristics 0,-1,1,2 gives .20,-.43,1.71,2.30.',
    'Each chosen upper neighbor is farther from the normalized input than its lower counterpart.'],
];
assert.equal(rows.length, 54);
assert.equal(learner.questions.length, 54);
assert.equal(learner.questions.reduce((n, q) => n+q.view.options.length, 0), 240);
const rowMap = new Map(rows.map(r => [r[0], r]));
assert.equal(rowMap.size, 54);

const issues = [
  {
    id: 'C5EX-VIEW-723A-GRAPH-BYPASS-FIRST',
    severity: 'revise', source_number: '723',
    question_id: 'q723-positive-powers',
    affected_items: ['view.options.A.text', 'view.options.C.text', 'view.options.D.text'],
    finding: 'Only one first-coordinate value passes elementary power bounds. The quantitative graph and all work on the second requested expression can be bypassed.',
    smallest_repair: 'Keep the source formulas and approved graph; replace only the competing paired estimates so plausible first-coordinate values do not uniquely identify the answer, and second-coordinate graph reading is discriminated. Recheck affected options/task fidelity, not the unchanged source/figure gates.',
  },
  {
    id: 'C5EX-VIEW-723CD-GRAPH-BYPASS-FIRST',
    severity: 'revise', source_number: '723',
    question_id: 'q723-small-and-product',
    affected_items: ['view.options.B.text', 'view.options.C.text', 'view.options.D.text'],
    finding: 'Only one first-coordinate value is in the elementary required range. No graphical estimate or combined-power calculation is needed for selection.',
    smallest_repair: 'Keep the source formulas and approved graph; revise only competing estimates to test quantitative graph normalization/reading and the product as well. Recheck changed options and their dependency on the approved graph.',
  },
];
const affected = new Map(issues.map(i => [i.question_id, i]));
const sourceNumbers = [...new Set(learner.questions.map(q => q.id.match(/^q(\d{3})-/)[1]))];
assert.equal(sourceNumbers.length, 43);
assert.deepEqual(sourceNumbers, seed.exercises.map(e => e.number));
const questionReviews = learner.questions.map((q, index) => {
  const r = rowMap.get(q.id);
  assert.ok(r, q.id);
  const [, trueLetters, fidelity, ...evidence] = r;
  assert.equal(evidence.length, q.view.options.length, q.id);
  const correct = [...trueLetters];
  assert.deepEqual(q.view.options.map(o => o.id), evidence.map((_, i) => String.fromCharCode(65+i)));
  assert.ok(correct.every(id => q.view.options.some(o => o.id === id)));
  assert.ok(q.view.mode === 'single' ? correct.length === 1
    : correct.length > 1 && correct.length < q.view.options.length, q.id);
  const issue = affected.get(q.id);
  const sourceNumber = q.id.match(/^q(\d{3})-/)[1];
  const usedFigures = [...new Set([...q.view.figure_ids, ...q.view.options.flatMap(o => o.figure_ids)])];
  const redundancyEvidence = ({
    'q683-constants': 'Separated from variable-domain question: six constant signs versus shifted-variable partition; neither asks for the same response.',
    'q691-family': 'The general two-base theorem differs from 692 intermediate-curve placement. Numerical examples are expressly not a restriction on all a,b.',
    'q692-middle': 'Unlike the two-base general theorem, this requires the specified third curve and rejects arithmetic-mean interpolation. The added common-point statement repeats a mathematical fact but not a distinct original task.',
    'q698-decreasing': 'Distinct decreasing/increasing root geometry, not a duplicate of the two-root increasing case.',
    'q707-reverse-domain': 'Converse recurrence proof/domain checks differ from the forward representation/zero-ratio obstruction. Explicit recurrence convention applies in both.',
    'q712-nesting': 'General nested identities also support later graph matching, but no keyed answer is exposed; calculating a value and identifying an all-real graph are distinct tasks.',
    'q721-tiled-set': 'The repeating equal-floor union is not the single rectangle or two strips in 720; mixed-tile and interior membership add distinct judgments.',
    'q723-positive-powers': 'Two distinct source quantities, not duplicate questions, but the second can be skipped because the first-coordinate bounds isolate one option.',
    'q723-small-and-product': 'Different source quantities from the first pair, but the combined-product response is not required to distinguish options.',
  })[q.id] ?? `The ${sourceNumber} mathematical response is distinct from neighboring source tasks; competing alternatives change a sign, value, domain, endpoint or general claim rather than repeat equivalent option text. Paired/column recognition has production losses recorded in task_fidelity.`;
  return {
    question_id: q.id, inspection_order: index+1, source_number: sourceNumber,
    view_canonical_sha256: canonical(q.view), used_figures: usedFigures,
    task_fidelity: { verdict: issue ? 'revise' : 'pass', evidence: fidelity },
    redundancy: { verdict: 'pass', evidence: redundancyEvidence },
    answer_leakage: {
      verdict: 'pass',
      evidence: q.id === 'q724-lookup-table'
        ? 'The visible table contains candidate values, not exact requested inputs or keyed results. Its normalization/nearest-cell rule is honest lookup scaffolding; choosing and shifting cells remains mathematical work.'
        : usedFigures.length
          ? 'Visible figures contain formula/stroke legends or unkeyed candidate geometry, not root markers, matched formula-to-option keys or supplied result annotations. Where the graph embodies the requested relationship, reading it is the intended recognition response; the separate graph-bypass fidelity issues are not relabeled secret-key leakage.'
          : 'Only visible source conditions, competing mathematical claims and definitions are supplied. No correctness marker, source-solving record, author rationale or keyed cross-question instruction appears. Assertions in other unkeyed options are not accepted as facts without checking.'
    },
    mathematics: {
      verdict: 'pass',
      independent_solution: `Reused source-${sourceNumber} derivation from the hash-frozen independent solve; independently evaluated this view's complete statements and all alternatives as recorded below. No author correct set consulted.`,
      correct,
      option_checks: q.view.options.map((o, i) => ({
        option_id: o.id, truth: correct.includes(o.id) ? 'correct' : 'incorrect',
        option_canonical_sha256: canonical(o), evidence: evidence[i],
      })),
    },
    mode_correctness: {
      verdict: 'pass', mode: q.view.mode, true_count: correct.length,
      evidence: q.view.mode === 'single'
        ? 'Exactly one complete alternative is true/compatible; no equivalent second true option.'
        : 'Complete independent true set has more than one but fewer than all options; native multiple selection is appropriate.',
    },
    issue_ids: issue ? [issue.id] : [],
  };
});

const sourceReviews = seed.exercises.map(e => {
  const questions = questionReviews.filter(q => q.source_number === e.number);
  const number = Number(e.number);
  let loss = 'Independent writing of the comparison, root, interval or decomposition is replaced by recognition of complete mathematical alternatives. No source number/value, sign or labeled part is silently omitted.';
  if ([687, 688, 691, 692, 693, 698, 699, 719, 720, 721].includes(number))
    loss = 'Freehand construction/explanation is replaced by interpretation of actual approved graph geometry. The relevant ordering, increments, crossings, regions, all-real continuation or boundary inclusion remain; no original PNG is invented.';
  if (number === 707)
    loss = 'Written two-direction proof/induction is replaced by verification of coefficient construction and recurrence/domain propositions. Positive-integer indexing and the broader recurrence definition are visibly declared; ordinary nonzero-ratio theorem, negative ratios and zero cases are distinguished. This conditional convention scope is accepted, not claimed to resolve every historical definition.';
  if ([713, 716, 717, 718].includes(number))
    loss = 'Free witness/counterexample production is replaced by evaluating genuine and nongenuine candidate witnesses. Universal truth, carries, strict boundaries and negative remainders remain mathematically discriminated.';
  if (number === 723)
    loss = 'Essential loss: graphical inverse/forward numerical reading and both paired source quantities need not be performed. Each pair is uniquely selectable by the first-coordinate elementary range; quantitative graph-based approximation is not discriminated. Both source pairs require affected option revision.';
  if (number === 724)
    loss = 'The actual original/retained-reference table and finer exponent precision are not tested. An explicitly new table provides nearest .01 exponent values with an approximate-equality rule; normalization, actual nearest-cell comparison and decade-characteristic addition remain. No historical-table identity is claimed.';
  return {
    source_number: e.number, independent_solution_record: { ...bind(sourcePath), section: `### ${e.number}` },
    question_ids: questions.map(q => q.question_id),
    coverage: {
      verdict: number === 723 ? 'revise' : 'pass',
      evidence: `Reviewed every permitted view and all its options for this source (${questions.length} question${questions.length > 1 ? 's' : ''}). ${questions.map(q => q.task_fidelity.evidence).join(' ')}`,
    },
    source_response_loss: loss,
  };
});

// Corroborate only the new candidate table and option witnesses, not the 43
// already-passed source solves.
const corroboration = [];
for (const [t, value] of [[.20,1.58489],[.21,1.62181],[.30,1.99526],[.31,2.04174],
                         [.57,3.71535],[.58,3.80189],[.71,5.12861],[.72,5.24807]]) {
  assert.equal(Number((10**t).toFixed(5)), value);
  corroboration.push({ kind: 'authored-table-cell', exponent: t, displayed_value: value, pass: true });
}
for (const [m, t, v, alternate] of [
  [1.594,.20,1.58489,1.62181], [3.73,.57,3.71535,3.80189],
  [5.174,.71,5.12861,5.24807], [2.001,.30,1.99526,2.04174],
]) {
  assert.ok(Math.abs(m-v)<Math.abs(m-alternate));
  corroboration.push({ kind: 'candidate-nearest-cell', mantissa: m, selected_exponent: t, pass: true });
}
const graphA = learner.questions.find(q => q.id === 'q723-positive-powers');
const graphCD = learner.questions.find(q => q.id === 'q723-small-and-product');
assert.ok(graphA && graphCD);
corroboration.push({
  kind: 'graph-reading-bypass', question: graphA.id,
  evidence: 'The first exact quantity is strictly between 1 and 1.95. Among .94,1.14,1.95,.39 only one satisfies these bounds; no graphical numerical work or second-coordinate discrimination is required.',
  pass: true,
}, {
  kind: 'graph-reading-bypass', question: graphCD.id,
  evidence: 'The first exact quantity is strictly between .0041 and 1. Among .026,39,.0027,.0026 only one satisfies these bounds; no graphical numerical work or product discrimination is required.',
  pass: true,
});

const record = {
  schema: 'C5Ex-independent-choice-view-FIRST-v1', stage: 'BLIND-VIEW-BEFORE-AUTHOR-KEYS',
  reviewer: { kind: 'independent_agent', identity: 'sole active independent C5Ex FIGURE + BLIND VIEW reviewer' },
  cwd: root, frozenAt: new Date().toISOString(), mode: '0444',
  source_solve_reused: bind(sourcePath), source_solve_recomputed: false,
  source_stage_answer_comparison: 'Parent states prior comparison PASS/no defects; its file was not opened in this stage.',
  seed: bind(seedPath), seed_canonical_sha256: canonical(seed),
  learner_view: bind(learnerPath), learner_view_canonical_sha256: canonical(learner),
  figures_first_freeze: bind(figurePath),
  new_figure_reviews: figureReview.figures.map(f => ({
    figure_id: f.figure_id, asset_path: f.svg.path, asset_sha256: f.svg.sha256,
    reviewer: { kind: 'independent_agent', identity: 'sole active independent C5Ex FIGURE + BLIND VIEW reviewer' },
    verdict: f.status.toLowerCase(), evidence: f.persisted_review,
  })),
  review_order: [
    'Verified source independent FIRST hash and reused all 43 solutions; read allowed raw/current JSON and seed.',
    'Actually opened each of the eight authorized images once; independently checked six figure specs/SVG/render bindings and froze the separate figure PASS record.',
    'Inspected all 54 permitted learner views and all 240 options without author keys; task fidelity/redundancy/leakage judged separately from the mathematics.',
    'Recorded complete independent truth sets, individual option evidence, unique-set/mode checks, source-response losses, graph coverage and concrete FIRST defects.',
    'Freeze at 0444 before any author correct-set comparison; canonical final key review is not written.',
  ],
  source_reviews: sourceReviews, question_reviews: questionReviews,
  issues, local_candidate_corroboration: corroboration,
  coverage: {
    source_exercises: 43, source_labeled_parts_reused: 127,
    source_range: '682-724', learner_views_inspected: 54, options_independently_judged: 240,
    independent_truth_sets_frozen: 54, unique_mode_correct_sets: 54,
    mathematical_questions_pass: 54, mathematical_options_checked: 240,
    fidelity_pass: 52, fidelity_revise: 2, source_coverage_pass: 42, source_coverage_revise: 1,
    new_figures_pass: 6, source_fig76_geometry_reused: true,
    key_fields_seen: 0, author_correct_set_comparisons: 0, omissions_silently_accepted: 0,
  },
  image_usage: figureReview.image_usage,
  original_failures_preserved: [
    'The earlier source-stage black transparent modern preview remains failed visual evidence; no rewrite of that FIRST source record.',
    'Both graph-bypass fidelity defects are preserved in this immutable FIRST record. Author work is not fixed by the reviewer.',
  ],
  outcome: 'revise', status: 'FAIL',
  limits: [
    'No author source solve, full draft, handoff, provenance, answer-author or answer comparison file opened.',
    'No canonical s10y-choice-review-v1/final path-bound key review is claimed. This learner-only freeze has no draft digest and cannot certify agreement with an unseen author key.',
    'The declared author limitations, distractor derivations and full coverage metadata remain unseen and require separate authorized comparison; independently observed response losses are recorded here.',
    'Path-only relocation of same SVG/spec does not require another mathematical/image gate, but final snapshot bindings must be updated under separate authorization.',
    'No new runtime render, source PDF, crop, screenshot, rerender or image payload after the eight-payload cap.',
  ],
  scope: 'Writes only in choice-review-FIRST/figures and choice-review-FIRST/view. Dirty concurrent work preserved; no install/git/DB/paid call/new worktree/branch/timer/skill modification/app/cross-chat action.',
  usage: { host_tokens: 'UNKNOWN', host_cost: 'UNKNOWN', external_API: 0, paid_calls: 0, model_service_calls: 0 },
};
assert.equal(record.question_reviews.flatMap(q => q.mathematics.option_checks).length, 240);
assert.equal(record.question_reviews.filter(q => q.task_fidelity.verdict === 'pass').length, 52);
assert.equal(record.source_reviews.length, 43);
const allBindings = [record.source_solve_reused, record.seed, record.learner_view, record.figures_first_freeze];
for (const b of allBindings) assert.equal(bind(b.path).sha256, b.sha256);
for (const f of figureReview.figures) {
  for (const b of [f.spec, f.svg, f.render, f.preview, f.persisted_review])
    assert.equal(bind(b.path).sha256, b.sha256);
}
const target = `${own}/choice-view-FIRST.record0444`;
fs.writeFileSync(target, JSON.stringify(record, null, 2)+'\n', { flag: 'wx' });
fs.chmodSync(target, 0o444);
console.log(JSON.stringify({
  path: path.resolve(target), sha256: bind(target).sha256, status: record.status,
  outcome: record.outcome, questions: 54, options: 240, mathematical_pass: 54,
  fidelity_revise: 2, issue_ids: issues.map(i => i.id),
  figures: 6, image_payloads: 8, mode: '0444', author_keys_seen: 0,
  host_usage: 'UNKNOWN', external_API: 0,
}));
